y constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier of the second term is not a constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+5\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=-3$ and ${c}_{2}=5,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353286 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353287 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353288 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353289 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1000 #edb/ref 17592186353290 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1041 "selection" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1104 #edb/ref 17592186353288 13194139535517 true] [17592186353285 1110 #uuid "5e5eaa75-672a-532b-b418-ef1e6247ed08" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353286 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353286 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535517 true] [17592186353286 1111 #uuid "1956de25-ad59-568f-84ee-1149b7cf8ddc" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353287 1034 "I only" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353287 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535517 true] [17592186353287 1111 #uuid "da8f500b-8344-5abd-a8c7-9caebaad1d3f" 13194139535517 true] [17592186353288 1034 "III only" 13194139535517 true] [1759